] [17592186504839 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + b)=λ(\\frac{1}{2})a+λ(1)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -2 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-2}{1} = -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a - 2b=-2(\\frac{1}{2}a + b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-2\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504840 1080 "-4" 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504840 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504840 1083 #uuid "f3077d42-9f95-5118-81b0-e2f6ad381a3b" 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504841 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504843 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504841 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504841 1071 "Given that $-24a + 6b$ and $λ(4a - b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504841 1072 #uuid "f58264c5-b24b-55b5-b334-1e81505cb790" 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504841 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(4a - b)=λ(4)a+λ(-1)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-24}{4} = -6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{6}{-1} = -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-24a + 6b=-6(4a - b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504842 1080 "-\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504842 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504842 1083 #uuid "f75d0b77-0554-5d4c-8d8f-338361e0988a" 13194139535446 17592186045443 true] [17592186504843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504743 13194139535